Read back a stored run report

Usage: rust-mutants report [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Whether to paint the output. `auto` paints a terminal that has not set `NO_COLOR`

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a terminal that has not asked to go without
          - always: Always
          - never:  Never
          
          [default: auto]

      --root <DIR>
          The workspace root. Defaults to the working directory

      --run <ID>
          The run, by its identity. Defaults to the newest

      --format <FORMAT>
          How to write it

          Possible values:
          - lines:    The lines a person reads
          - json:     The stored `rust-mutants/run-report` document, verbatim
          - html:     One self-contained HTML page
          - stryker:  The mutation testing report every Stryker reader understands
          - junit:    The JUnit XML a continuous integration server already reads
          - sarif:    The findings as SARIF 2.1.0, for a code scanning view
          - markdown: The summary a person puts in a pull request
          
          [default: lines]

      --output <FILE>
          Write it here rather than to standard output

      --tui
          Read it at the terminal instead of writing it

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
